-- Test: the flat-scope fallback is ambiguous when several sibling sections
-- define the name (spec §3.3.4 as corrected 2026-09-04, §5.1).
--
-- The reference below is at top level: neither § a nor § b is on its
-- ancestry, so resolution falls back to the flat scope, where BOTH x's are
-- candidates of the same type. That is a genuine ambiguity, and it must be
-- reported AT THE REFERENCE (line 11) — not at either definition — naming
-- each candidate together with the section that defines it, so the reader
-- can see which qualified spelling (a.x or b.x) to use.

f MEANS x

§ a
x MEANS 1

§ b
x MEANS 2

#EVAL f
